    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "314d0c11_3ebc0620",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T14:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If uniforms can have two different layouts, we unfortunately need two different gatherers. Right now this gatherer is used by both ExtractPaintData (which feeds into the `shadingSsboTracker` instance that is configured to use either SSBOs or UBOs based on `caps()-\u003estorageBufferPreferred()`), or ExtractRenderStepData (which always uses UBOs).\n\nAlternatively, since the gatherer (and its UniformManager under the hood) are only long-lived so we can reuse the high-water allocation, we could have resetting allow it to change its layout, so ExtractPaintData() would set the gatherer\u0027s layout and similarly for ExtractRenderStepData. It\u0027s a little more plumbing but I kind of favor that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f33f66a6_d2cfa2ea",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T19:16:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can certainly implement that but I wonder if the gatherer really needs to be long-lived? Most of its members are stack allocated counters which always get reassigned on `reset()` and the only heap-allocated member that\u0027s not debug-only (`SkTextureDataBlock::fTextureData`) gets reset by the Extract functions.\n\nI worry about the statefulness in letting `ExtractPaintData` and `ExtractRenderStepData` mutate the layout being used by the gatherer under the hood. Could they instantiate their own function-scope gatherers with the appropriate layout instead, especially if they are going to reset the gatherer on every call anyway?",
      "parentUuid": "314d0c11_3ebc0620",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55666bcb_1ac7f8d4",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T19:23:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AIUI the goal here is to keep using the same `fStorage` in UniformManager instead of letting it be freed and reallocated over and over again. (`SkTDArray` is like a `vector` in that it never shrinks when cleared. The idea is that, over time, `fStorage` converges on a mostly steady-state, large-enough size.)",
      "parentUuid": "f33f66a6_d2cfa2ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ecaa07d1_784512ae",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T22:04:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. Could we perhaps decouple the UBO/SSBO encoding part of UniformManager from the backing storage? This code here could initialize a `SkTDArray` (with some heuristic-based initial size) and the `Extract*` helpers can create one-off `SkPipelineDataGatherer`s over the preallocated storage.\n\nAlternately, if we must maintain the existing model then I would introduce a function like `setLayoutAndReset(Layout)` and call that as the first thing in the helpers (or perhaps before calling out to the helpers, so they don\u0027t have to worry about which layout to select).",
      "parentUuid": "55666bcb_1ac7f8d4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf53a041_911293bc",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T22:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That sounds like Michael\u0027s original suggestion to me, I think? _\"... we could have resetting allow it to change its layout, so ExtractPaintData() would set the gatherer\u0027s layout and similarly for ExtractRenderStepData. It\u0027s a little more plumbing but I kind of favor that.\"_",
      "parentUuid": "ecaa07d1_784512ae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ddfe238_eb1d91fa",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 451,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T22:22:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a slight nuance in that currently the helpers are responsible for resetting the gatherer _after_ they have written to it. They will now need to reset it before (and maybe after). Though personally I think the initial layout reset should be done at the call site instead of having the helpers also know about which layout they need to apply on the gatherer.\n\nI\u0027ll work this change to demonstrate what I mean. If folks like the idea to decouple the storage from the gatherer then I can rework that in a follow up.",
      "parentUuid": "cf53a041_911293bc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 451,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 451,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
