      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T14:34:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apple does hard-spec layouts, though? e.g.: https://screenshot.googleplex.com/3fqy8BTcdFPcShv",
      "parentUuid": "aa9e5942_7df0a2d6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74aa93b2_937fedbc",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ResourceTypes.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T14:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But our kMetal is that plus additional rules, if I remember correctly. My understanding had been that the metal layout rules weren\u0027t complete, and so we had to make choices for some of the vector types. Given that it seems even more important to comment that `kMetal` isn\u0027t just Apple\u0027s spec.\n\nOr maybe their spec is complete now, and we should just align to that and be able to claim `kMetal` is exactly the hard-spec.",
      "parentUuid": "020cdbec_28ffb3f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5331e2ef_c4a61ef9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ResourceTypes.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T14:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we are claiming additional layout rules beyond Apple\u0027s rules, that\u0027s news to me and we should document it a lot more than this comment :) You might be right, though. I wasn\u0027t involved in the initial design of layouts.",
      "parentUuid": "74aa93b2_937fedbc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f76a619a_e931e7e3",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ResourceTypes.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T15:52:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did some digging in the current code and I can\u0027t actually find any differences. It may be that Ganesh has some special handling, but graphite does not any more (and maybe never did, or it\u0027s been made consistent in the recent refactorings to UniformManager).\n\nOne thing I did notice was that the `RulesMetal` struct/template is identical to the `Rules430` struct. Perhaps we don\u0027t even need a `kMetal` in the Layout enum any more?\n\nRegardless of that decision, I withdraw my thinking that the comment has value. It\u0027s 100% stale at this point and should be removed like John suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "5331e2ef_c4a61ef9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28a73bee_97bafa23",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ResourceTypes.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-01T15:57:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Metal does have one uniform-related rule that std430 doesn\u0027t have; it encodes half types in fp16 format.\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/skia/skia/+/main:tests/graphite/UniformManagerTest.cpp;l\u003d54-57;drc\u003da5ef003835c77ce0ef6cafe994400fe937031ae2",
      "parentUuid": "f76a619a_e931e7e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1be9d75c_7b648f2f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/ResourceTypes.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 51,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T19:16:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed the size of the half-precision types is the only nuance between std430 and our Metal layout rules that I\u0027m aware of. As long as that\u0027s worth keeping I think we should retain the `kMetal` enum but I\u0027m happy to remove the comment if you don\u0027t think it adds value.\n\nIf there are any differences with the \"standard\" Metal layout then we should document them. FWIW the unit tests (https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tests/graphite/UniformOffsetCalculatorTest.cpp;l\u003d74?q\u003dUniformOffsetCalculatorTest\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fskia%2F) are fairly self-documenting in that regard.",
      "parentUuid": "28a73bee_97bafa23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 51,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 51,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "6f484989f359985bd5381656c9a3c5a589442aab",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
